rastructure requirements at scale","via":["text","textcolumn"]}]}],"via":["section"]}]}],"via":["section aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12"]},{"t":"section","c":"bg-color relative section md:py-8 py-6 py-0","r":[0,488,360,2338],"s":{"pos":"relative","pad":"24px 0px"},"k":[{"t":"div","c":"relative container contain mx-auto","r":[0,512,360,2274],"s":{"pos":"relative","pad":"0px 16px"},"k":[{"t":"div","c":"row grid-12 xs:grid-12 sm:grid-12 md:grid-12 lg:grid-12 xl:grid-12 flex-wrap md:flex","r":[16,512,328,2274],"k":[{"t":"div","c":"md:cols-9 md:pl-0 md:pr-32 free-text","r":[16,512,328,2140],"k":[{"t":"div","c":"press-release-header heading5","r":[16,512,328,44],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 16px"},"k":[{"t":"span","c":"press-release-location","r":[16,511,204,24],"f":"Roboto 20px/22px 500 capitalize rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"SANTA CLARA, Calif. -"},{"t":"span","c":"press-release-formateddate","r":[16,511,302,46],"f":"Roboto 20px/22px 500 capitalize rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"September 15, 2026"}],"via":["announcement","press-release-template capitalize"]},{"t":"div","c":"textcolumn","r":[16,572,328,2080],"k":[{"t":"p","r":[16,572,328,192],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"As AI moves from experimentation to deployment, organizations are confronting a new infrastructure reality: while compute cycles are temporary, the data AI creates continues to accumulate. As that data compounds, the ability to store, manage and access it economically is becoming a critical consideration for long-term AI success."},{"t":"p","r":[16,784,328,168],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"At AI Infrastructure Summit, September 15-17 in Santa Clara, Calif., Tim Rausch, SVP of HDD Development at WD, will discuss how AI is reshaping infrastructure requirements and why economically scalable capacity is emerging as a foundational element of the AI era.","inner":"a"},{"t":"p","r":[16,972,328,96],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"The session builds on findings from the recently released IDC white paper, sponsored by WD, Built for Scale: The Enduring Role of HDDs in the AI Era, which found that:","inner":"a"},{"t":"ul","r":[16,1088,328,208],"s":{"pad":"0px 0px 0px 16px","mar":"20px 0px"},"k":[{"t":"li","r":[32,1088,312,72],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1088,312,72],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"61% of surveyed organizations experienced data growth of 25% or more over the past year due to AI"}]},{"t":"li","r":[32,1180,312,48],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1180,312,48],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"74% expect data volumes to grow 25% or more over the next three years"}]},{"t":"li","r":[32,1248,312,48],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1248,312,48],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"85.4% reported growth in data lake volumes over the past 12 months"}]}]},{"t":"p","r":[16,1316,328,240],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"During the keynote, Rausch will share WD’s vision for helping customers manage AI’s growing data footprint while balancing capacity, performance, power efficiency and economics at scale. He will also discuss innovations designed to support the next generation of AI infrastructure as organizations seek to retain more data, derive more value from it and scale AI with confidence."},{"t":"ul","r":[16,1576,328,204],"s":{"pad":"0px 0px 0px 16px","mar":"20px 0px"},"k":[{"t":"li","r":[32,1576,312,24],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1576,312,24],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"WHAT: Reinventing Storage for AI at Scale","inner":"b"}]},{"t":"li","r":[32,1620,312,48],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1620,312,48],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"WHO: Tim Rausch, SVP, HDD Development, WD","inner":"b"}]},{"t":"li","r":[32,1688,312,24],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1688,312,24],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"WHEN: Sept. 16, 2026 | 3:50pm","inner":"b"}]},{"t":"li","r":[32,1732,312,48],"s":{"disp":"list-item","mar":"0px 0px 12px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","k":[{"t":"p","r":[32,1732,312,48],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"WHERE: AI Infrastructure Summit | Santa Clara, Calif. | Main Stage","inner":"b"}]}]},{"t":"p","r":[16,1800,328,168],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"In addition to the keynote, WD will showcase its enterprise storage portfolio in booth # 605. The demos will highlight how WD is helping hyperscalers, CSPs, neo clouds and data center customers achieve the capacity, efficiency, and economics required for AI infrastructure at scale."},{"t":"p","r":[16,1988,328,96],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"Source: IDC White Paper, Sponsored by Western Digital Corporation, Built for Scale: The Enduring Role of HDDs in the AI Era, Doc. #US54789026, September 2026.","inner":"b i"},{"t":"p","r":[16,2104,328,312],"s":{"mar":"0px 0px 20px"},"f":"Roboto 16px/24px 400 rgb(0, 0, 0)","text":"WD, also known as Western Digital, builds the storage infrastructure that powers certainty in the AI-driven data economy. At the forefront of innovation, WD partners with the world's leading hyperscal","k":[{"t":"b","r":[16,2106,72,19]},{"t":"a","r":[16,2394